            <ArticleTitle>Distinct association of SLC19A1 polymorphism -43T&gt;C with red cell folate levels and of MTHFR polymorphism 677C&gt;T with plasma folate levels.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>174-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVES" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">The role of SLC19A1 -43T&gt;C, MTHFR 677C&gt;T and MS 2756A&gt;G polymorphisms on red cell and plasma folate levels.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="DESIGN AND METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">Genotype analysis of the three polymorphisms. Red cell and plasma folate measurements in 64 patients with coronary artery disease.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">The non-wild type allele of SLC19A1 polymorphism -43T&gt;C was associated with low red cell folate levels and the non-wild type allele of MTHFR polymorphism 677C&gt;T with low plasma folate levels.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">SLC19A1 and MTHFR genes are differently associated with red cell and plasma folate levels.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
